From 9771fa00ba14a9514a6d26832a35b8b92547d6d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amelie Delaunay <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jan 2025 16:22:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1497/1695] dts: stm32: add Unique device ID (UID) for
 stm32mp21

Unique device IDentifier (UID) is 96 bits and is defined in OTP5-7, as:
OTP5 UID[31:0] Unique ID bits,
OTP6 UID[63:32] Unique ID bits,
OTP7 UID[95:64] Unique ID bits.

It is used by ADAC (Authentication Debug Access Control) to respond to
ADAC_DISCOVERY_CMD, used by the debugger to request some information about
the target.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git fbbebbefccbbeffeeb3d5512e3a5f908643568da dts: stm32: add Unique device ID (UID) for stm32mp21]
Signed-off-by: Amelie Delaunay <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
